  "id": "polygenic-inheritance",
  "term": "polygenic inheritance",
  "definition": "Polygenic inheritance is a pattern in which a condition is influenced by the combined effects of many genetic changes rather than a single gene. In this packet, schizophrenia is described as mainly following this kind of inheritance, with contributions from common genetic variants and some copy number changes.",
